<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06HD">Remark <span data-tag="06HD">9.4.2.10</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compactly generated, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete. Then the restriction functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}^{(\kappa ,\lambda )-\operatorname{c}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{&lt; \kappa }, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{&lt; \kappa } ) \quad \quad F \mapsto F|_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{&lt; \kappa } } \]
</div>
<p> is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. Here $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ denote the full subcategories spanned by the $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact objects of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, respectively. See Proposition <a data-tag="067B" href="/tag/067B">9.4.1.11</a>. </p>
</article>
